WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.534
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.167
Guys, before we get started,

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.868
does anyone here want to be
Speaker of the House?

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.300
[ Laughter and cheers ]

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.367
Yep, as of tonight's taping,
it's been three days and

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:14.567
nine votes, and we still don't
have a Speaker of the House.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:15.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.501
Before today's vote,
C-SPAN was like,

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:18.801
"We swear this is not a rerun."

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:20.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.834
Right now, Kevin McCarthy is
so embarrassed, he went up to

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.100
George Santos and said, "Help me
create a new identity."

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.067 --> 00:00:29.434
McCarthy has lost nine times.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:31.467
It is brutal.
I mean, there's a reason why

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:32.868
you only get three strikes
in baseball.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.467
I mean, it's just hard to watch.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:37.200
Nine? That's a lot.
That's somewhere between

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.133
COVID variants
and "Yellowstone" spin-offs.

00:00:39.133 --> 00:00:41.133
Nine. Nine.

00:00:41.133 --> 00:00:43.701
And get this -- I read that some
Democrats and Republicans are

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:47.634
considering a deal for a speaker
both parties can get behind.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.801
-Ooh.
-So congratulations to our new

00:00:49.801 --> 00:00:51.367
Speaker of the House,
"Top Gun: Maverick."

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:52.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:52.934 --> 00:00:54.400
That's a good movie.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:00.300
Meanwhile, McCarthy is now
in the negotiation phase

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.667
where he's making a bunch of
concessions with the Republicans

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.133
who are against him,
and one of those concessions is

00:01:05.133 --> 00:01:08.434
a change to the rules that would
make it easier to remove him.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.567 --> 00:01:13.868
You know it's bad when the only
way you can get hired is

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:17.033
if you promise to get fired,
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:19.033
'Course, with everything going
on in Washington, it's been

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.634
a busy week for news anchors,
and I think they need a break.

00:01:21.634 --> 00:01:23.167
I mean, check out this clip of

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.767
Andrea Mitchell on MSNBC
earlier today.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:28.267
-After a night spent offering
big concessions

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:30.701
to the never-Kevins, at the risk
of alienating

00:01:30.701 --> 00:01:33.968
some of his original supporters
in the Republican caucus --

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.534
[ Gags ]
Excuse me.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:36.267
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.300
-Hey! Hey!

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.133
Wow.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:42.334
[ Rim shot ]

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:47.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.834
-And then, for the first time
in TV history,

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:51.501
a news anchor coughed up
a hair ball.

00:01:51.501 --> 00:01:53.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.767
That's the sound you make when
the doctors checks if you have

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.501
strep throat,
you know what I'm saying?

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:59.300
That's the sound
your ketchup bottle makes

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:00.968
when you try to squeeze out
the last drop.

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:03.501
The closed captioning just
said... --

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:09.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:12.067
Yep, Congress spent a third day
voting for

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:14.300
a new Speaker of the House,
and after so many rounds, I feel

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.701
bad for the people who have to
keep reading all the names of

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.234
the representatives
to get their vote.

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:21.067
-[ Scoffs ] You know what?
Don't feel bad. It's easy.

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.901
-I'm just saying it's tedious.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:24.334
And some of the names are hard
to pronounce.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.667
-Not when you're a professional
announcer like me.

00:02:26.667 --> 00:02:28.534
Go ahead, test me.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:31.534
-Okay, I guess I can.
I'll test you real quick.

00:02:31.534 --> 00:02:32.834
Who's this?

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:33.901
-Okay, easy.

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:35.234
Jheri Curl.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:36.234
-Alright.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.968 --> 00:02:40.501
Okay, who's this?

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.701
-Come on. Barry Manilow.
Come on.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:43.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.567
Give me some harder ones.
Rapid-fire me.

00:02:45.567 --> 00:02:47.834
-Okay. Here we go.
Who's this?

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.434
-Okay. David Schwimmer.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:50.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:53.200
Rihanna.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.734
Lady Macbeth.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:57.167
Bad Salmon.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:58.200
Chips Ahoy.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:02:59.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.267
Frank Stallone.

00:03:01.267 --> 00:03:03.067
Ah-ah-ah-choo.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.601
Oh, it's Scott Delivery,
it's DiGiorno.

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:09.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:13.067
Ah-na-na-na-na, na-na-na,
na-na-na, na-na-na.

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
Na-na-na-na-nah.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.501
♪ Lyrical gangster ♪

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:18.701
[ Applause ]

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.467
Nice Blunt Rotation.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:21.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:24.000
Oh, Yank Johnson.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.300
Menage a Trois in Greece.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.634 --> 00:03:30.434
Oh, Vicious Sharts. Ooh.

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:31.868
And Liar.

00:03:31.868 --> 00:03:33.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:36.033
-Thank you very much.
Steve Higgins, a professional.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.234
Steve Higgins, everyone.

00:03:37.234 --> 00:03:42.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.434
Everyone is weighing in on this.

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:47.934
Today, Elon Musk tweeted, "Kevin
McCarthy should be Speaker."

00:03:47.934 --> 00:03:49.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:51.534
It makes sense 'cause Kevin
McCarthy is a lot like a Tesla.

00:03:51.534 --> 00:03:53.167
He was on the road to
his destination and then

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.501
suddenly veered off course.

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:57.868
Meanwhile, President Biden
is staying out of

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:00.767
the Speaker drama, calling it
embarrassing but saying,

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:02.100
"That's not my problem."

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:03.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:04.100
Then he added...

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:20.868
[ Applause ]

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.434
Biden then added...

00:04:34.801 --> 00:04:39.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:40.834
Then he added...

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:56.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.067
At which point Biden just posted
the Kermit drinking tea meme.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.467
There you go.
That's interesting.

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.801
[ Applause ]

00:05:03.801 --> 00:05:05.400
Everybody's talking about this.

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:08.467
In his forthcoming book, Prince
Harry claims that Prince William

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:12.000
once knocked him to the floor
during an argument about Meghan.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.434
[ Audience oohs ]

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.968
Apparently the fight happened at
the Buckingham Waffle Palace.

00:05:15.968 --> 00:05:20.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.968 --> 00:05:22.634
It's fun when royals fight

00:05:22.634 --> 00:05:24.100
'cause they keep their pinkies
out.

00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:26.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:28.133
Harry was shocked because
usually when they fight,

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:30.734
they just stand back and tell
their butlers what to do.

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:32.267
"Now, perhaps a knee
to the groin."

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:33.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:34.701
"Choke him out, Jeeves."

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:38.834
Harry also writes
in his new book that before

00:05:38.834 --> 00:05:41.701
he married Meghan, William and
Kate were religious viewers

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.834
of her show "Suits."

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:46.300
I feel like I believed
everything Prince Harry said

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:47.367
until just now.

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:50.634
I don't think even
the stars of "Suits"

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.234
were religious viewers of
"Suits."

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:53.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:56.300
Well, some movie news --
"Avatar: The Way of Water" has

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.868
officially passed
"Top Gun: Maverick"

00:05:57.868 --> 00:06:00.334
to become
the number-one movie of 2022.

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:02.567
It is a huge, huge hit.

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:05.334
It made us wonder, what would
other classic movies look like

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:07.133
if they took place underwater?

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:08.567
Check this out.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:13.868
[ Burbling ]

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:15.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:15.834 --> 00:06:17.534
-There you go. That's it.

00:06:17.534 --> 00:06:19.400
Pretty good. I'd watch that.

00:06:20.467 --> 00:06:22.968
Well, listen to this -- I heard
that people on TikTok are

00:06:22.968 --> 00:06:25.534
claiming that a great way
to beat the flu is

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:28.968
by sleeping with
potato slices in your socks.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:32.434
There's a lot of questionable
medical advice online,

00:06:32.434 --> 00:06:33.567
and depending on where you look,

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:34.868
you get pretty different
answers.

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:37.133
For instance, for the flu,
TikTok says...

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.200
Facebook says...

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:44.367
WebMD says...

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:49.667 --> 00:06:52.334
Next up, for a cold,
TikTok says...

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.133
Twitter says...

00:06:57.634 --> 00:06:58.734
WebMD says...

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:04.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:04.667 --> 00:07:06.801
And finally, for COVID,
TikTok says...

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:10.501
Truth Social says...

00:07:11.801 --> 00:07:13.234
And WebMD says...

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:17.200
I think just call a real doctor.

00:07:20.701 --> 00:07:22.634
Guys, I read about
a new COVID variant

00:07:22.634 --> 00:07:23.801
that has some people worried.

00:07:23.801 --> 00:07:27.467
It's called XBB.1.5.

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:29.801
I guess they couldn't think of
a catchier name.

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:32.901
And it actually inspired me
to write a tiny song.

00:07:32.901 --> 00:07:34.467
Roots?
♪♪

00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:40.400
♪ There was Alpha, then Delta ♪

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.968
♪ Then Omicron next ♪

00:07:41.968 --> 00:07:45.534
♪ But this latest variant
might be the best ♪

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:49.133
♪ It's XBB.1.5 ♪

00:07:49.133 --> 00:07:52.467
♪ Another brand of COVID-19
has arrived ♪

00:07:52.467 --> 00:07:54.267
♪ It's a new strain ♪

00:07:54.267 --> 00:07:56.234
♪ But it isn't the same ♪

00:07:56.234 --> 00:07:59.601
♪ Sounds more like
Elon Musk's kid's name ♪

00:07:59.601 --> 00:08:03.167
♪ It's XBB.1.5 ♪

00:08:03.167 --> 00:08:06.934
♪ Not UB40,
who sings "Red Red Wine" ♪

00:08:06.934 --> 00:08:10.501
♪ Put on your mask when
you're inside a facility ♪

00:08:10.501 --> 00:08:13.901
♪ It could be a robot from
a "Star Wars" trilogy ♪

00:08:13.901 --> 00:08:17.434
♪ It's XBB.1.5 ♪

00:08:17.434 --> 00:08:20.968
♪ Not OMG or MP3 or TCBY ♪

00:08:20.968 --> 00:08:24.434
♪ Or an eye chart made by
a really high guy ♪

00:08:24.434 --> 00:08:28.000
♪ Sounds like the password of
your parents' Wi-Fi ♪

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:31.901
♪ It's XBB.1.5 ♪

00:08:31.901 --> 00:08:35.467
♪ XBB.1.5 ♪

00:08:35.467 --> 00:08:41.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:41.968 --> 00:08:50.534
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:52.801
That's the most applause
I've gotten in five years.

00:08:52.801 --> 00:08:54.267
-Wow.
-Unbelievable.

00:08:54.267 --> 00:08:57.868
Switching gears, a big consumer
electronics show just kicked off

00:08:57.868 --> 00:09:00.634
in Las Vegas, and there are so
many new products on display,

00:09:00.634 --> 00:09:03.834
including a self-driving
stroller that's powered

00:09:03.834 --> 00:09:05.834
by artificial intelligence.

00:09:05.834 --> 00:09:08.868
[ Laughter ]

00:09:08.868 --> 00:09:10.367
The only question is, will it be

00:09:10.367 --> 00:09:12.968
a billion-dollar lawsuit or
a trillion-dollar lawsuit?

00:09:12.968 --> 00:09:14.067
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.067 --> 00:09:15.267
Yeah, the commercial says,

00:09:15.267 --> 00:09:17.567
"Order one now before
we all get arrested."

00:09:17.567 --> 00:09:19.534
But don't worry. It comes with
an override button

00:09:19.534 --> 00:09:21.801
in case your baby needs to take
control of the stroller.

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.968 --> 00:09:24.868
Another interesting product
being unveiled is

00:09:24.868 --> 00:09:28.033
the high-tech,
snore-silencing pillow.

00:09:28.033 --> 00:09:30.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:33.167
Although that's any pillow
if you hold it against

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:34.934
someone's face long enough,
you know what I'm saying?

00:09:34.934 --> 00:09:37.200
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.033
A pillow that stops you from
snoring, which has got to be

00:09:40.033 --> 00:09:42.167
the most passive-aggressive gift
of all time.

00:09:42.167 --> 00:09:45.701
[ Laughter ]

00:09:45.701 --> 00:09:47.567
Stop.

00:09:47.567 --> 00:09:50.968
And finally, a 19-year-old just
travelled nearly 2,000 miles

00:09:50.968 --> 00:09:53.734
from Maine to Florida
on a unicycle.

00:09:53.734 --> 00:09:54.801
[ Audience oohs ]

00:09:54.801 --> 00:09:56.300
And much like his wheel,

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:58.467
it's a pretty safe bet
that he's single. Yeah.

